# Put the held object down on the table: on the free spot nearest the robot (mode free), or with
# its centre at a target (relative, metric, anchor).

# "free" (also when empty): the free spot nearest the robot in `region`. "relative": x and y from
# -1 to 1 across the table's workspace, where +-1 is as far as the object still sits fully on it. "metric": x and
# y in metres from the workspace's centre. "anchor": x and y in metres from the centre of the object
# `anchor` names, found on the table. x points to the right and y away, as seen from the robot's
# base (base_link's -y and +x axes).
string mode
float64 x
float64 y

# Free mode: part of the table to use, as seen from the robot: "any" (the whole work area, the
# skills' workspace.* parameters), "left", "middle" or "right" (its thirds across).
string region

# A target that is taken: the object goes to the nearest free spot at most this far from it, in
# metres; 0 uses the server's place.tolerance_m. Refused when none is free.
float64 tolerance_m

# The object's long axis from the table's x axis, in degrees, when use_yaw is true (a long axis
# looks the same after half a turn). Otherwise any heading the wrist reaches.
bool use_yaw
float64 yaw_deg
# How far the heading may be off, in degrees; 0 uses the server's place.yaw_tolerance_deg.
float64 yaw_tolerance_deg

# Anchor mode: what to find on the table, as it looks to SAM 3.1 ("red cube").
string anchor
# Anchor mode: where the anchor is (e.g. an earlier place_pose), so the match nearest it is taken;
# an empty frame_id: the best match.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped anchor_pose
---
bool success
string message

# Where the object was set down, in the robot's base frame: its centre on the table, its long axis as the x axis;
# valid only when success is true.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped place_pose

# On a failure: the arm is still down at the table or the object; back off before anything else.
bool arm_stuck
---
# "finding_anchor", "finding_spot", "moving_above", "descending", "releasing", "retreating"
string phase
